ST_TITLE:['{N} & {F}: The Brave Adventure','{N} & {F}: Best Friends','{N} & {F}: The Sharing Picnic','{N} & {F}: The Tidy-Up Game','{N} & {F} vs. the Cavity Bugs','{N} & {F}: The Starlight Journey'],
ST_OPEN:['Once upon a time, {N} lived in {P}. {N} had the brightest laugh you ever heard.','The sun was smiling one morning. In {P}, {N} stretched big and looked out the window.','In {P} lived a very special child — curious, sparkly {N}.','One sunny day, {N} held Mom\'s hand and went on an outing to {P}.'],
ST_MEET:['Then a tiny sound came from the bushes. "Hi! I\'m {F} the {T}!" {N} was surprised, but soon waved hello.','As {N} walked along, someone gently tapped {N}\'s shoulder. It was a cute {T} named {F}. "Will you be my friend?"','A sparkly light flashed, and there stood {F} the {T}. "{V}, I\'ve been waiting for you!"'],
ST_THEME:{
'Courage':['{F} said, "Over that hill grow rainbow berries. But there\'s a dark cave on the way, and I\'m scared to go alone."','{N} felt a little scared too. But {N} really wanted to help {F}. "It\'s okay — let\'s go together!"','The cave was very dark. {N} took a big breath and counted: one, two, three. Little by little, {N}\'s heart felt calm.','"When we\'re scared, let\'s sing!" {N} sang a happy song, and {F} sang along. The song bounced around the cave walls.','At last, a bright light shone at the end of the cave. Rainbow berries in seven colors hung everywhere.','"{V}, you are so brave!" said {F}. {N} smiled shyly, and learned that courage means taking one step even when you\'re scared.'],
'Friendship':['{N} and {F} played happily all day. But then they argued about who would ride the swing first.','"Me first!" "No, me first!" Their faces turned red, and they turned their backs on each other.','Sitting alone, {N}\'s heart felt achy. Swinging alone wasn\'t any fun at all.','{N} bravely walked over to {F}. "I\'m sorry about before. Let\'s take turns." {F} nodded. "I\'m sorry too."','They pushed each other on the swing. Every time they flew up high, giggles filled the air.','{N} kept it close in heart: "I\'m sorry" and "thank you" are magic words that bring friends back together.'],
'Sharing':['{N} took a yummy strawberry cookie out of the bag. But {F} was looking at it with a hungry face.','{N} thought for a moment — there were only two cookies. "Hmm… one is for you!"','{F}\'s eyes went round, and then came a big smile. "Thank you! Then I\'ll share half my apple with you."','Shared, the cookie and the apple tasted twice as good. Squirrels and birds gathered too, and a little picnic began.','When everyone shared a little, every tummy was full and every heart felt warmer.','{N} learned that sharing doesn\'t make things smaller — it makes joy bigger.'],
'Tidying up':['{F} came to play in {N}\'s room. But toys and books were scattered everywhere.','"Huh? Where did my blue block go?" {N} searched and searched but couldn\'t find it.','{F} said, "Let\'s play the tidy-up game! We find a home for every toy!"','Dolls to the basket house, books to the shelf house, blocks to the box house! They sang as they tidied, one by one.','When they finished, the blue block popped out from under the bed: "Here I am!" The room felt big and fresh.','{N} promised, "After playing, I\'ll help my toys find their homes!" The toys seemed to sparkle with joy.'],
'Healthy teeth':['After a yummy dinner, sleepy {N} said, "I\'ll skip brushing tonight and just go to bed…"','Just then {F} appeared with a tiny magnifying glass. "{V}, the cavity bugs are about to throw a party in your teeth!"','Through the glass, little bugs cheered, "Yum yum, no brushing tonight!" {N} was shocked.','{N} grabbed a toothbrush and brushed up and down, inside and out — scrub, scrub! The bugs ran away screaming.','Teeth sparkled white in the mirror. {F} gave a big thumbs-up. "Awesome! You\'re a strong-teeth knight!"','That night, {N} slept sweetly with a fresh mouth. Brushing every night is a great promise to keep your body safe.'],
'Bedtime':['It was late at night, but {N} couldn\'t fall asleep. The moon peeked in through the window.','Then {F} came with a soft cloud blanket. "{V}, want to go stargazing?"','They floated up into the sky on the cloud blanket. One by one, the stars twinkled hello.','The stars asked {N} to share one good thing from the day. {N} told them about helping a friend.','The stars clapped, and sparkly dust drifted down and gently closed {N}\'s eyes.','Soon {N} was fast asleep under a cozy blanket. {F} whispered, "Good night. See you tomorrow."']
},
ST_END:['From that day on, {N} and {F} were the very best of friends. Tonight in dreams, they\'ll hold hands and play in {P} again. The End.','As the sky turned sunset-gold, {F} waved. "{V}, today was so much fun. Let\'s play again!" {N} came home with a warm heart. The End.','{N} happily told Mom and Dad all about the day. Mom and Dad gave {N} the biggest hug. The End.'],
