CT.en.PNOTE=["Lots of other people are enjoying their meal at a restaurant too. If you run around, you could get hurt by hot food. Waiting in your seat makes the food taste even better.", "Everyone else needs the bathroom just as much as you do. Taking turns lets everyone use it comfortably. If it's really urgent, you can politely ask, \"May I go first?\"", "Lots of tiny germs we can't see hide on our hands. Washing with soap bubbles for 30 seconds, even between your fingers, helps stop colds. Clean hands protect you and your friends.", "Some people on the bus are tired and want to rest. Talking quietly helps everyone ride comfortably. And don't forget to hold on tight.", "When you say hello first, the other person feels happy and so do you. A greeting says, \"I'm glad to see you.\" Let's look them in the eye and say hello with a smile.", "If we don't brush, leftover food between our teeth can cause cavities. Brushing up and down after meals keeps teeth strong. Let's smile brightly with clean teeth.", "Toys have homes too, and they're happy when they go back to their place. Tidying up means you can find them quickly next time. Shall we race to see who tidies up fastest?", "Different foods give our bodies different kinds of strength. Let's try just one bite of a new food first. Eating a bit of everything helps you grow tall and strong.", "When someone helps you, they're sharing their kindness. Just saying \"thank you\" answers that kindness. Let's always say our thanks out loud.", "Everyone makes mistakes. What matters is the courage to say \"I'm sorry\" first. A real apology helps you and your friend smile again.", "A library is where everyone quietly travels inside books. Whispering and tiptoeing protects your friends' journeys. Let's put books back where they belong when we're done.", "Cars can be faster than we think and appear suddenly. Even on green, raise your hand and look left and right before crossing. Holding Mom or Dad's hand is even safer.", "Water is a precious gift from rivers and seas. Using a cup when brushing saves lots of water. The water we save helps protect the Earth.", "Our bodies grow while we sleep. Going to bed early means more fun tomorrow morning. Let's talk about today and fall asleep together.", "Teachers are kind people who teach us so many things. Saying \"Hello!\" first makes your teacher very happy. Let's bow a little and greet them cheerfully.", "In a classroom full of friends, taking turns is important. Raising your hand and waiting lets everyone be heard. Waiting is a wonderful thing to learn too.", "Presenting in front of others takes courage and can feel scary. Listening to the end gives your friend lots of strength. Let's clap and say it's okay to make mistakes.", "Running in the hallway can make you bump into a friend at a corner. Walking gently on the right keeps everyone safe. Going slowly won't make you late.", "Everyone is hungry at lunchtime, so taking turns matters. Lining up makes sure everyone gets their fair share. The waiting makes lunch taste even better.", "Your friend's things are precious to them. Taking them without asking can upset and worry your friend. Let's always ask, \"May I borrow this?\"", "Pushing your chair in keeps friends from tripping over it. It's a small thing, but it makes the classroom much tidier. Let's push it in every time we stand up.", "Your teacher shares important things we need to know. Sitting nicely and looking at them helps you remember better. Let's save playing for break time.", "Grandmas and grandpas sometimes find heavy bags hard to carry. Asking \"Can I help?\" makes them very happy. A little help brings a lot of joy.", "Giving with two hands shows \"I respect and care for you.\" Let's give things to elders politely with both hands. Grandpa will smile from ear to ear.", "Police officers always look after our safety. When you see one, let's say \"Thank you!\" If you ever get lost, you can ask a police officer for help.", "Restaurant workers are someone's precious family too. Saying \"please\" and \"thank you\" makes everyone feel good. Kind words make kind hearts.", "Delivery workers carry heavy boxes all the way to our home. One \"thank you\" can give them energy. Let's share our thanks with people who work for us.", "Shots sting a little, but they keep our bodies strong. The doctor is working hard to make you better. If you're scared, hold Mom's hand and be brave.", "Riding the cart or pushing it fast can bump into other people. Babies and grandparents shop at the market too. Shall we push slowly and shop together?", "It's natural to want lots of things. But choosing only what we promised today is great practice. If you talk instead of whining, Mom and Dad can listen better.", "Samples are meant for many people to have a little taste. Taking just one and saying \"thank you\" lets others try too. A sharing heart tastes the best.", "At the movies, everyone gets lost in the story together. Talking loudly can stop others from hearing the movie. Let's chat about it when it's over.", "Kicking the seat in front startles and bothers that person. Keeping your feet on the floor lets everyone watch comfortably. Think how you'd feel if you sat in front.", "Museum objects are very old and can break easily. Looking without touching lets future friends see them too. Let's read the signs together if you're curious.", "A museum is a place where many people enjoy things quietly. Talking softly helps everyone focus. You can share how you feel out loud once we're outside.", "The floor around a pool is very slippery when wet. Running can lead to a bad fall. Walking slowly means more time for fun.", "Showering before swimming keeps the pool water clean. Warming up keeps our bodies from getting a shock. Let's all have fun in clean water.", "On the subway, people need to get off first to make room. Waiting before getting on keeps everyone quick and safe. Let's stand aside by the door and wait.", "The subway shakes when it starts and stops. Holding on tight keeps you from falling. Let's save playing for after we get off.", "A seatbelt holds us tight if the car stops suddenly. We wear it even for short trips. When it goes \"click,\" we're ready to go!", "Many people spend a long time together on a plane. Kicking seats or being noisy makes it hard for everyone. Let's pass the time drawing or reading.", "If you fall off a bike, you could hurt your head. A helmet is a strong hat that protects your head. Wearing one makes you an even cooler rider.", "Scooters can go fast, so riding on the road is very dangerous. Let's ride slowly in safe places like the park. Don't forget your helmet and pads!", "If we cross where there's no crosswalk, drivers might not see us. Even if it's a little farther, crossing at the crosswalk is safer. Safety comes first.", "In a parking lot, cars can move suddenly and drivers can't easily see kids. Hold Mom or Dad's hand tight while walking. Let's play hide-and-seek at the playground instead.", "A blinking light means it will soon turn red. Running across could make you trip. Waiting for the next green light is the really cool choice.", "In a fire, elevators can stop, so they're dangerous. Take the stairs and cover your nose and mouth with a wet cloth. Smoke rises, so stay low.", "Even if a stranger offers something yummy, never go with them. Shout \"No!\" and come straight to Mom or Dad. Keeping you safe is the most important thing.", "On the phone, people can't see your face, so how you speak matters more. Answering politely with \"Hello?\" makes the caller feel good. If you don't know them, pass the phone to Mom or Dad.", "Everyone sometimes wants time alone. Knocking and asking \"May I come in?\" shows respect. Mom and Dad will knock on your door too.", "Waiting for elders to start eating shows thanks and respect. Saying \"Thank you for the food\" makes the table feel warm. Let's enjoy our meal together.", "Bringing your dishes to the sink is a big help to Mom and Dad. Our family is a team that helps each other. And don't forget to say \"That was yummy!\"", "Spoons and chopsticks have pointy ends and can hurt if we play with them. Let's promise to use them only for eating. Using chopsticks well makes your fingers clever too.", "Talking with food in your mouth can make food fly out or make you choke. Chew well, swallow, then talk. Eating slowly helps your tummy too.", "Sharing something yummy makes everyone at the table happy. Joy has a magic that grows when it's shared. Let's all say \"Yummy!\" and smile.", "Anyone can spill by accident. When you tell us honestly instead of hiding it, Mom and Dad are really proud. Wiping it up together makes it clean in no time.", "Water on the bathroom floor can make us slip and fall. Let's keep water play inside the tub. You can have fun with bath toys there.", "Germs in your mouth can hurt your teeth while you sleep. Brushing well before bed lets your teeth rest too. Mom or Dad will check them one last time.", "Putting clothes in the basket makes laundry much easier. Your room stays clean and it helps Mom and Dad. Our home is a place we all take care of.", "Making your bed in the morning starts the day fresh. Taking care of your own space is a wonderful habit. Shall we fold the blanket together today?", "Lining up shoes keeps the entryway tidy and makes them quick to put on. Guests can come in feeling welcome too. Let's turn the toes toward the door.", "Hanging up your coat keeps it from wrinkling so it's ready next time. It's a great way to take care of your things. Let's practice using a hanger together.", "Sorting trash turns it into things we can use again. Let's keep plastic, paper and cans separate. You can be a little hero who protects the Earth.", "Turning off lights saves electricity and helps the Earth. Let's make a habit of clicking the switch when we leave a room. Small actions add up to big help.", "Watching TV too close makes your eyes tired quickly. Let's sit back and watch only for the time we agreed. Afterwards, let's go play outside.", "Phones are fun, but too much screen time tires your eyes and mind. Stopping on your own when time's up is really cool. Let's spend the rest of the time playing as a family.", "Looking at a phone while walking means you might not see people or cars coming. Look ahead when walking, and stop if you need to look. Safety comes first.", "It's natural to feel upset when you lose a game. But saying \"That was fun!\" makes you a truly great friend. You can always try again next time.", "When a friend asks you to play, it means they like you. Answering kindly warms their heart too. What shall we play together today?", "A new friend might feel nervous and lonely at first. Saying \"Hi! Want to play?\" first means a lot to them. Having the courage to make friends is wonderful.", "A gift carries the heart of the person who chose it. Even if you don't love it, let's say \"Thank you!\" That kindness is the biggest gift.", "A birthday is a very special day for your friend. Saying \"Happy birthday!\" makes them so happy. Let's celebrate their happy day together.", "Grabbing a friend's toy really hurts their feelings. Asking \"Can we play together?\" lets you both have fun. Waiting your turn is kind too.", "Sharing things makes playtime more fun than playing alone. Saying \"Let's share!\" makes your friend happy. A sharing heart helps friendship grow.", "When a friend tells you a secret, it means they trust you. Keeping it brings you closer. But if it's something dangerous, you must tell a grown-up.", "When a friend cries, their heart is hurting. Just asking \"Are you okay?\" can be a big comfort. Staying quietly beside them helps too.", "Winning feels great, but the friend who lost may feel sad. Saying \"That was fun, let's play again!\" makes everyone happy. Thinking of your friend's feelings is the real win.", "When everyone wants a turn, taking turns lets us play without fighting. If you let others go first, they'll do the same for you. Your turn will always come.", "Little ones can't yet say how they feel, so they sometimes cry. Comforting them kindly makes them love their big brother or sister even more. You're such a dependable big sibling.", "Feeling upset is natural, but pushing could hurt your little sibling. Let's use words like \"Please be careful next time.\" Shall we redraw the picture together?", "Family members who are studying need quiet time. Playing quietly on your own is a really big help. When they're done, let's have fun together.", "Waiting patiently when Mom and Dad are busy means a lot. Asking \"Can I help?\" helps us finish faster so we can play together. You're our home's wonderful helper.", "Greeting guests warmly makes our home feel even cozier. Even if you're shy, a simple \"Hello\" is enough. A smile makes guests feel happy too.", "Grandma and Grandpa have been missing you so much. Saying hello and hugging them first makes them so happy. TV can come after the greetings.", "Picked flowers wilt quickly and others can't enjoy them. Let's enjoy them with our eyes and take a photo. Flowers are prettiest when they stay in the ground.", "Signs tell us the promises that protect a place. Let's keep the promise so the grass doesn't get hurt. Reading signs together can be fun too.", "Puppies can get scared when a stranger rushes up to them. Let's ask the owner, \"May I pet your dog?\" first. Gently offering the back of your hand is a nice hello.", "Even tiny lives like ants are as precious as ours. If we watch instead of stepping on them, we can see what they're doing. Nature is our friend that lives with us.", "Trash left at the sea can hurt fish and turtles. Let's take home the trash we brought. That way we can play at a clean beach again!", "The forest is home to many animal friends. Walking quietly lets us hear birds and the wind. Shall we listen to the sounds of the forest?", "Leaving the tap running lets lots of water go to waste. Filling a cup helps save water. By saving water, you're protecting the Earth.", "A mask keeps your cold germs from reaching your friends. Even if it feels stuffy, let's wear it for them. If you rest well, you'll feel better soon.", "Coughs and sneezes spread germs far. Covering with your elbow keeps them from reaching friends. It protects both you and your friends.", "Medicine helps when we're sick, but taking it the wrong way is dangerous. Even if it looks like candy, only take it when a grown-up gives it. Ask Mom or Dad if you're curious.", "Hiding an injury can make it hurt more. Telling us right away means we can take care of it quickly. You're really brave for telling the truth.", "Litter makes our neighborhood dirty, and animals may eat it and get sick. Keep it in your pocket and throw it in a bin. We make our neighborhood clean.", "Good sleep helps both body and mind grow. Going to bed on time makes mornings feel fresh. Tomorrow will be an even more exciting day.", "A morning greeting warmly opens the family's day. \"Did you sleep well?\" makes everyone smile. Who will say good morning first today?", "Packing your own bag helps you get ready without forgetting anything. It's a great habit that grows your independence. Mom and Dad will check with you at first.", "Saving your pocket money lets you buy what you really want. Let's put half in the piggy bank and plan how to use the rest. Enjoy watching your savings grow."];
/*PN-END*/
